  "in_scope": [
    "Enumerate the P2-reachable surface closure from IOI's canonical surface and catalog registrations, content-bind that enumeration, and carry it as the gate's subject; a claim traversing a surface outside the bound enumeration is refused, not waived.",
    "Join exactly two subordinate checks over that closure: p2-surface-provenance-integrity-check (provenance and origin truth of what a reachable surface presents) and p2-launcher-catalog-availability-check (the launcher compiles from IOI's canonical catalog and omits or honestly marks unavailable anything not operationally bound). The join is a conjunction — both retained literals must be present and bound to the same closure revision, and this gate names them in dependency_work_item_ids rather than adopting them as aggregate children, because aggregate closure is stage-exit machinery and this gate closes no stage.",
    "State the rule source-neutrally and verify it that way: the check detects any prohibited residue on a reachable surface, from any origin, rather than matching a fixed list of names. A name list is admissible only as a non-authoritative triage aid and never as the pass condition.",
    "Refuse when a subordinate check passes only because its subject was narrowed — a surface dropped from the closure, or the launcher removed from the P2 profile — unless the profile record itself names the removal.",
    "Evaluate the launcher against the exact disposition recorded in launcher_disposition. While the disposition is `included`, the launcher is inside the bound closure and its bar is a canonical IOI catalog, IOI-owned taxonomy, and honest availability — never a proof that the application estate is complete; unbound applications may be omitted or rendered visibly unavailable. A disposition of `excluded` is admissible only when every recorded removal condition is satisfied, including the updated closure digest and the passing negative-reachability verifier; a failing check and inconvenient remediation are both explicitly not grounds."
  ],
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Unreachable internal or reference material: research corpora, capture archives, verifier fixtures, and any surface no P2 journey can reach. Their existence in the repository is not a finding.",
    "Properly licensed and attributed third-party dependencies. External origin is not prohibited; their notices stay in place, and reporting one as a finding is itself a gate defect.",
    "Proving that every application the launcher can list is implemented. The gate bounds what a reachable surface may present and claim, not the operational depth of the application estate.",
    "Any repository-wide sweep, any legal or trademark clearance, and any claim about surfaces outside the bound closure.",
    "P1 and P3. This gate and its closing record carry P2's selected-profile obligation only; nothing here is added to the M9 aggregate that closes P1, P2, and P3 together."
  ],
